  manatee: { breathEvery: [3600, 6e3], firstBreath: [600, 2400], breathFor: [40, 80], breathDepth: 0.6, up: 12, riseTimeout: 400, grazeEvery: [600, 1400], afterBreath: [100, 300], grazeFor: [200, 400], near: 8, search: 6, searchTries: 12, depth: 16, downTimeout: 400, retry: 300, reach: 0.05, drift: 0.2, pace: { rise: 0.08, down: 0.06 }, seagrassComfortCap: 55 },
  // Since 0.1.133 the abyss is made with the world by the BP's features/trench_* (generated by gen133/features133.py,
  // its numbers there: abyss -40 give or take 8 over 90 and 2 over 12, the cliff from 46 in four ledges, canyons to
  // -56, spires in 12-block cells capped at y 28) and the digging job below no longer runs; these numbers are the
  // 0.1.132 design it follows. The Places text and the spawns still use `biome`.
  // The Deep Trench (0.1.130; dug into an abyss since 0.1.132: world/trench.js, trenchRules.js and abyssRules.js). Each
  // column in the biome is dug down to `abyss` (give or take abyssVary over abyssScale, and `rough` over roughScale):
  // some 100 blocks of water. Where the biome ends the floor drops at a cliff: a column `edge` blocks from the nearest
  // 4 by 4 cell outside the biome (that edge bent by up to rimJag over rimJagScale) is dug toward the abyss from rimTop
  // (above the sea floor), all the way by `rim` blocks in (at most 16: the chunks round are all that's looked at), part
  // of the drop in `ledges` steps wandering over ledgeScale, the cliff's face rough by up to `crag` blocks over cragScale.
  // Canyons cut deeper: lines joining points on a grid every `cell` blocks (each joined
