      late: ["It's dark! Is it night? It's night! Bedtime for Aloof! Night night!"],
      lost: ["I can't go that way. I tried. Twice. I'll wait here and suck my thumb."],
      found: ["You found me! I was hiding! I wasn't hiding. I was standing. Hee hee!"],
      hello: ["Hiya! Hi! Hello! I said it three times so it counts more!", "Oh! It's you! I forgot you were you! Hi!"],
      home: ["This is my house! There's a bed in it. And me. Hee hee.", "Welcome! Don't mind the drool. It's decorative."],
      leaving: ["Going to the zoo! To see the monkeys! I love them! I hate them! Let's go!", "Zoo time! I'm going to laugh at everything. Even the rocks."],
      visiting: ["Look! A monkey! I love it! No wait, I don't. Yes I do!", "Hee hee hee! That one did a funny thing! I didn't see it. Hee hee!"],
      returning: ["I'm home! Did I go somewhere? I went somewhere! It was great!", "Back home. I saw monkeys today. They were wonderful. And terrible."],
      asleep: ["Zzz... monkeys... yay... boo... yay... zzz..."],
      waiting: ["My house fell over! Or some of it did. I'll wait here. I'm good at waiting. I'm waiting now!"],
      likes: ["I like sucking my thumb, drooling, laughing, and monkeys! Monkeys are the best!", "Laughing is my favourite. Hee hee! See? I'm doing it right now!"],
      dislikes: ["I don't like books, learning, bunnies or monkeys. Monkeys are the worst!", "Bunnies. Something about the ears. They're listening. They're always listening."],
      pleased: { "monkeys": ["I saw the monkeys today! They're my favourite! Best day ever!"] },
